  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Preserving a Key Jaguar Corridor through SMART Conflict Management and Community Engagement in the Buffer Zone of the Laguna de Terminos Protected Area</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to support the preservation of a key wildlife corridor between the Laguna de Terminos Protected Area and the Calakmul Biosphere Reserve in Campeche by increasing tolerance for jaguars among human residents. This project is intended to conserve the jaguar by empowering select local residents to patrol their communities for illegal activities, reducing conflict between jaguars and cattle ranchers, and educating communities about the value of the jaguar. Specific activities include: (1) camera-trapping studies conducted by local Monitoring Committee (MC) members in three communities to ensure long-term wildlife monitoring; (2) training of MC members in the use of the Spatial Monitoring and Reporting Tool (SMART) for jaguar-cattle conflict mitigation to reduce illegal activity, cattle predation, and attendant jaguar killings); and (3) educational workshops in three communities to increase awareness of jaguar conservation issues and increase positive attitudes toward jaguars.</narrative>
  </description>
